# The same board, which reaches into its left chart and hands what it holds to the right one itself:
# `self.right.take(self.left.fig, self.left.ax)`. The call runs on the board through `right` and fills `fig` and `ax` with
# the board through `left.fig` and `left.ax` (#172): `take` sets the fields of the right part to those of the left part,
# fields a chart keeps its figure in, the board's `left` and `right` each holding a Chart (`Node::holds`, #173). The right
# part holds the left part's figure, and the screen shows one, as on the clean side; what differs is who reads the left
# chart's fields: the board's own call, not the chart's `lend`.

